# Direction — TOOTRIPSY (Nikhil Gupta)

One-line: *Apple-keynote restraint over a drone reel.* The site behaves like a
film title sequence: the brand is the headline, the work is the argument, the
kit is the proof, the inquiry is two minutes.

## Pattern inherited from the Jalen build (~/chepheww)

- Same stack (Next.js static export, S3 + CloudFront, basic-auth gate, SES inquiry API).
- Same structure: brand-first hero → story-led work → proof → kit → inquiry → his footer.
- Same law: real photos first, sourced numbers only, nothing on the page that
  confesses it is anything but finished.

## Deliberate departures (the Taste Card, not the template)

| | Jalen | Nikhil |
|---|---|---|
| Temperature | warm tungsten, candlelight | cool blue-black, glacier |
| Type voice | Newsreader serif, light | Archivo grotesk, 800–900, tight |
| Motion | a dimmer that warms the page | settle + parallax; the loop does the moving |
| Accent | tungsten #C98A3D | aerial cyan #3FB9CF, sampled from his pools |
| Booking | dinner request (6 steps) | brand inquiry (4 steps, package-anchored) |
| Press layer | /press + one-pager | /kit — media kit with published packages |

## Voice rules

- Minimal, confident, short lines. No agency-speak, no adjectives doing the
  work his frames already do.
- His own words where possible: "storytelling, motion, and aerial
  perspectives" is his Collabstr bio, promoted to a headline.
- Never name a place or client beyond what his public profiles state.

## What the site must never do

- Show a stat that isn't in research/nikhil-brief.md or content/site.ts.
- Show a stock frame. Every image is his (agency/asset-sources.md).
- Carry any draft/review language, credit line, or process note.
