/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html:24:<section class="feasts" id="spots" aria-labelledby="spots-title"><div class="wrap feasts-lead"><div><p class="chapter">04 · Festus Feasts</p><h2 id="spots-title">The restaurant<br>is the main character.</h2><p class="lead">Not a drive-by review. A seat with the owner. A close-up on the food. A reason to return.</p></div><figure><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="assets/conversation-480.9878c9a538b8.webp 480w, assets/conversation-800.ccb2d6c0b5d0.webp 800w, assets/conversation-1200.3102f51e6cf6.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) calc(100vw - 40px), 720px"><img src="assets/restaurant-conversation.d27969530270.jpg" width="1800" height="1200" alt="Festus listening across a shared table at 9JaGrills" loading="lazy"  decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>A shared table at 9JaGrills, Oakland. Carolyn Fong / The SF Standard.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="wrap feast-editorial"><figure><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="assets/egusi-480.ea63067db2a1.webp 480w, assets/egusi-800.f3c23e6b7d1f.webp 800w, assets/egusi-1200.a90361ffedeb.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) calc(100vw - 40px), 480px"><img src="assets/festus-egusi.68ec487dbc04.jpg" width="1200" height="1800" alt="Festus tasting Nigerian food at 9JaGrills in Oakland" loading="lazy"  decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>Festus tastes egusi and fufu at 9JaGrills.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">Oakland · Nigerian cooking</p><h3>A taste of home.</h3><p>Festus Feasts follows the restaurants that give the Bay its character—and makes room for the people behind them.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/05/14/festus-ezeli-festus-feasts-bay-area-food/">Read the reported story ↗</a></div><figure><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="assets/spread-480.6eecee1d3dd8.webp 480w, assets/spread-800.4ef537230c72.webp 800w, assets/spread-1200.1c2a68a42c32.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) calc(100vw - 40px), 480px"><img src="assets/table-spread.ff14fa25f7e6.jpg" width="1200" height="1800" alt="Nigerian dishes on a shared table at 9JaGrills" loading="lazy"  decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>Nigerian dishes laid out for a shared meal.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="wrap discovery"><aside class="home-ground"><p class="eyebrow">The Bay route</p><p>Save a stop and make a short table plan. The map is editorial, not literal.</p><div class="city-filters js-only" role="group" aria-label="Filter restaurant stops"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-city="all">All</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-city="San Francisco">San Francisco</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-city="Oakland">Oakland</button></div></aside><div class="restaurant-list"><p class="small" id="filter-status" role="status">Four places to begin.</p><article class="stop" id="stop-four-kings" data-location="San Francisco"><div class="stop-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Chinatown</p><h3>Four Kings</h3></div><button class="save-stop js-only" type="button" aria-label="Save Four Kings to your table plan" aria-pressed="false">Save</button></div><p>Singaporean chili crab and milk bread feature in Festus’s Chinatown visit.</p><a class="text-link stop-source" href="https://festusezeli.com/festus-feasts/hidden-heat-in-chinatown-four-kings-delivers-a-royal-feast/">Read the visit ↗</a><details><summary>The assist</summary><div class="assist">Tell them Festus sent you.</div><p class="small">An invitation to support the restaurant. No discount, priority access or partnership is implied.</p></details></article><article class="stop" id="stop-buttercup" data-location="Oakland"><div class="stop-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Oakland</p><h3>Buttercup Diner</h3></div><button class="save-stop js-only" type="button" aria-label="Save Buttercup Diner to your table plan" aria-pressed="false">Save</button></div><p>A family business, and the college sweethearts behind it.</p><a class="text-link stop-source" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ya-zmdgik3Y">Watch the visit ↗</a><details><summary>The assist</summary><div class="assist">Tell them Festus sent you.</div><p class="small">An invitation to support the restaurant. No discount, priority access or partnership is implied.</p></details></article><article class="stop" id="stop-9jagrills" data-location="Oakland"><div class="stop-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Downtown Oakland</p><h3>9JaGrills</h3></div><button class="save-stop js-only" type="button" aria-label="Save 9JaGrills to your table plan" aria-pressed="false">Save</button></div><p>Nigerian cooking and a conversation at the table: a close look at Festus’s food work.</p><a class="text-link stop-source" href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/05/14/festus-ezeli-festus-feasts-bay-area-food/">Read the feature ↗</a><details><summary>The assist</summary><div class="assist">Tell them Festus sent you.</div><p class="small">An invitation to support the restaurant. No discount, priority access or partnership is implied.</p></details></article><article class="stop" id="stop-chotto" data-location="San Francisco"><div class="stop-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">Union Square</p><h3>Chotto Matte</h3></div><button class="save-stop js-only" type="button" aria-label="Save Chotto Matte to your table plan" aria-pressed="false">Save</button></div><p>The setting for Dine with an NBA Champion, Festus’s Airbnb Original.</p><a class="text-link stop-source" href="https://www.airbnb.com/experiences/7137152">Explore the dinner ↗</a><details><summary>The assist</summary><div class="assist">Tell them Festus sent you.</div><p class="small">An invitation to support the restaurant. No discount, priority access or partnership is implied.</p></details></article><div class="table-plan js-only"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your table plan</p><p id="plan-status" role="status">Save a stop to make a list for later.</p></div><button class="button" type="button" id="copy-plan" disabled>Copy your stops</button><textarea id="plan-fallback" aria-label="Your table plan — select and copy" readonly hidden></textarea></div></div></div></section>
