/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html:26:<section class="media wrap" aria-labelledby="media-title"><figure><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="assets/action-480.b567976628af.webp 480w, assets/action-800.8712d100eecd.webp 800w, assets/action-1200.d29d7de39308.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) calc(100vw - 40px), 720px"><img src="assets/warriors-action-2013.deea38d7e986.jpg" width="3555" height="2028" alt="Festus Ezeli in uniform during a Golden State Warriors game in 2013" loading="lazy"  decoding="async"></picture><figcaption>Festus in uniform, 2013. Matthew Addie / CC BY 2.0.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="chapter">05 · Broadcaster, founder, student</p><h2 id="media-title">Player perspective.</h2><p class="lead">At NBC Sports Bay Area, Festus frames Warriors basketball from lived experience. That same perspective now informs a platform connecting restaurants, creators, brands and communities.</p><p>Festus Feasts began by sending attention to local restaurants. The founder vision is larger: turn storytelling into durable opportunity without losing the people and neighborhoods that made the stories matter.</p><div class="education"><p class="eyebrow">Education</p><div class="education-lockups"><a class="hbs-mark" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/festusezeli_harvardbusinessschool-executiveeducation-activity-7479633657205370880-Qi_O"><strong>Harvard Business School</strong><span>Executive Education</span><small>Business of Entertainment, Media, and Sports</small></a><a class="vanderbilt-mark" href="https://festusezeli.com/about-festus/"><strong>Vanderbilt University</strong><span>Economics</span><small>The foundation before the league</small></a></div></div><div class="credential-list"><a class="credential" href="https://www.nba.com/warriors/news/warriors-to-play-los-angeles-clippers-play-in-tournament-20260412"><strong>NBC Sports Bay Area ↗</strong><span>Warriors pregame and postgame analyst</span></a><a class="credential" href="https://festusezeli.com/about-festus/"><strong>ESPN ↗</strong><span>NBA analyst, as listed in his official biography</span></a><a class="credential" href="https://www.cbsnews.com/sanfrancisco/news/festus-feasts-former-golden-state-warrior-bay-area-food-scene/"><strong>CBS San Francisco ↗</strong><span>Festus Feasts and the Bay Area food scene</span></a><a class="credential" href="https://video.kqed.org/video/north-beach-restaurant-house-of-nanking-bon-delire-e75upg/"><strong>KQED ↗</strong><span>Check, Please! Bay Area appearance</span></a></div></div></section>
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html-27-
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html:28:<section class="dine" id="dine" aria-labelledby="dine-title"><div class="wrap dine-grid"><div class="place-setting" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><b></b><span></span></div><div><p class="chapter">06 · Union Square</p><h2 id="dine-title">Dine with Festus.</h2><p class="lead">A full meal. A cultural co-host. A table built for conversation.</p><p>Hosted by Festus Ezeli at Chotto Matte for up to 15 guests. Airbnb handles current availability, pricing, eligibility and reservations.</p><a class="button primary" href="https://www.airbnb.com/experiences/7137152" data-event="dinner_booking_click">Check dinner availability <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html-29-
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html:30:<section class="proof wrap" aria-labelledby="proof-title"><div><p class="chapter">07 · Selected proof</p><h2 id="proof-title">Credibility,<br>without the résumé wall.</h2></div><div class="proof-grid"><article><b>Warriors</b><span>Pregame and postgame analysis</span></article><article><b>100K+</b><span>Festus Feasts community</span></article><article><b>HBS</b><span>Business of Entertainment, Media, and Sports</span></article><article><b>Africa</b><span>Basketball as an economic ecosystem</span></article></div></section>
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html-31-
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html:32:<section class="work" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title"><div class="wrap work-grid"><div><p class="chapter">08 · Build something together</p><h2 id="work-title">Bring Festus<br><em>into the room.</em></h2><p>For producers, brands, restaurants and event organizers looking for a credible voice with a real point of view.</p><a class="button light" href="https://festusezeli.com/contact/" data-event="business_contact_click">Contact Festus’s team <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="media-note">Festus’s official contact page handles submission.</p></div><div class="pathways"><article><span>01</span><h3>Media + broadcast</h3><p>Analysis, hosting, interviews and on-camera storytelling.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Brand partnerships</h3><p>Food, culture, sport and community-led campaigns.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Speaking + events</h3><p>Resilience, leadership, reinvention and global opportunity.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Restaurant features</h3><p>Prepare the restaurant name, location, founder story and what makes the table matter.</p><a href="#book" data-category="Restaurant feature">Create a restaurant brief ↓</a></article></div></div></section>
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html-33-
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html:34:<section class="shop wrap" id="shop" aria-labelledby="shop-title"><div><p class="chapter">09 · The goods</p><h2 id="shop-title">Food is love.<br><em>Wear it out.</em></h2></div><div><p>Official Festus Ezeli merchandise. MerchLabs handles current products, prices, sizing and fulfillment.</p><a class="button quiet" href="https://merchlabs.com/collections/festus-ezeli" data-event="merch_collection_click">Shop the collection ↗</a></div></section>
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html-35-
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html:36:<section class="book" id="book" aria-labelledby="book-title"><div class="wrap booking-grid"><div><p class="chapter">10 · Prepare the introduction</p><h2 id="book-title">Make the first<br>message useful.</h2><p>This is a mockup site. If you like it, we can connect the finished site to your domain and email. For now, this brief is created locally; nothing entered here is submitted or stored.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://festusezeli.com/contact/">Skip to the official contact page ↗</a></div><form id="inquiry-form" class="js-only" novalidate><label for="category">What brings you here?</label><select id="category" name="category" required><option value="">Choose a category</option><option>Media appearance</option><option>Brand partnership</option><option>Restaurant feature</option><option>Speaking engagement</option><option>Private experience</option><option>General inquiry</option></select><p class="field-context" id="category-context">Choose what brings you to the table.</p><label for="name">Your name</label><input id="name" name="name" autocomplete="name" maxlength="120" required><label for="message">What should Festus’s team know?</label><textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" maxlength="3000" required></textarea><p id="form-error" class="form-error" role="alert"></p><button class="button primary" type="submit">Create my inquiry brief <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><div id="brief-result" hidden><p role="status">Your brief is ready. It has not been sent or stored.</p><label for="brief">Copy this into your message</label><textarea id="brief" readonly rows="6"></textarea><button class="button" type="button" id="copy-brief">Copy inquiry brief</button><a href="https://festusezeli.com/contact/" class="text-link">Open official contact page ↗</a></div></form></div></section>
/Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/release/index.html:37:<section id="privacy" class="privacy wrap"><details><summary>Privacy, media and photograph credits</summary><p>This site stores no form submissions, analytics identifiers or personal data. Embedded media loads only when requested. Contemporary photographs are credited to Carolyn Fong / The San Francisco Standard; historical photographs retain their stated licenses.</p></details></section>
