/Users/zacfaber/nikhil-gupta-mock/research/nikhil-brief.md:22:TASTE CARD (Skill 001 — Creator Site):
/Users/zacfaber/nikhil-gupta-mock/research/nikhil-brief.md:23:1. HERO: the visual that most immediately communicates his identity = a sweeping cinematic drone/aerial frame (coastline, city, or resort from above). If it doesn't read "cinematic travel creator for brands" in one second, it's the wrong hero. Anti-rule: no generic stock travel photo, no smiling-headshot hero.
/Users/zacfaber/nikhil-gupta-mock/research/nikhil-brief.md:24:2. VISUAL DIRECTION: derive from his grid — cinematic, cool-toned, minimal, Silicon-Valley polish (Apple-keynote restraint: big imagery, sparse type, lots of air). This is the deliberate contrast with Jalen (dark/warm/editorial). Anti-rule: do not copy Jalen's palette or layout — same flare (confidence, restraint, one accent), different world.
/Users/zacfaber/nikhil-gupta-mock/research/nikhil-brief.md:25:3. SECTIONS from his strongest content pillars: (a) Selected work / destinations — story-led features of his best shoots, like Festus's spots but places and brand shoots; (b) Aerial — drone work as its own showcase; (c) Brands — hotels/airlines/destinations he creates for (only what his public profile supports); (d) Media kit — follower count + services for brand buyers; (e) Inquiry — one clean contact path (email + form-style CTA) for brand work.
