# KO Fitness rebuild

## Coaching intake agent

The Coaching page includes a mobile-first intake chat. Set the API endpoint when
building the site:

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_INTAKE_API_URL=https://YOUR_API.execute-api.REGION.amazonaws.com/intake npm run build
```

The AWS backend is defined in `infra/template.yaml` (SAM/CloudFormation): API
Gateway HTTP API, Python Lambda, on-demand DynamoDB table, Bedrock Claude access,
and SES notification permission. Deploy with verified SES sender/recipient values:

```bash
sam build --template-file infra/template.yaml
sam deploy --guided --parameter-overrides \
  KyleEmail=kyle@example.com SesFromEmail=intake@example.com \
  AllowedOrigin=https://your-site.example
```

Bedrock model access must be enabled in the deployment region, and SES identities
must be verified (both addresses while the account is in the SES sandbox).

Run the complete application simulation without AWS or credentials:

```bash
python3 backend/local_test.py
```

Static marketing site for KO Fitness, built with Next.js App Router and Tailwind CSS.

## Run locally

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

## Static export

```bash
npm run build
```

The exported site is written to `out/` via `output: "export"` in `next.config.mjs`.

## Instagram feed hook

`components/InstagramFeedSlot.tsx` is the documented integration seam for the Road to IRONMAN Instagram feed. Pass normalized `InstagramPost[]` data into the component when an approved feed source is available. Until then, it renders a clearly labeled `FEED-SLOT` placeholder.

## Preview deployment (Oct 19, 2026)

- Preview: https://preview.d2lp9muyf525c9.amplifyapp.com (Amplify app `d2lp9muyf525c9`, branch `preview`, manual zip deploy)
- Intake API: stack `kofitness-intake`, `https://efavz8z3w7.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/intake`, model `global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`
- Demo routing: `KyleEmail` and `SesFromEmail` are zacfaber@icloud.com (SES sandbox). Swap them for Kyle's address after it's verified and SES production access is granted.
- `app/(intake)` (/start) is the Faber Solutions intake source and is stripped from KO builds: `rm -rf out/start` before zipping.
- Original images live in `assets-src/`; `public/images` holds the WebP versions.
