### /Users/zacfaber/festus-feasts-definitive/RESEARCH.md
# Festus Feasts research and match ledger

Research date: 2026-10-26. Public facts were checked directly against the linked pages. Follower counts are snapshots, not timeless claims.

## Identity card

- **Palette:** restaurant wood, cream plates, leafy green, glove blue, and championship gold recur across the current grid; the latest Xica, Dumpling Bites, Mandalay, and Oakland Style posts supplied the working color sample. [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/festusfeasts/)
- **Type energy:** arena-scale condensed weight for his 6'11" presence, paired with terse scoreboard mono; warm and direct rather than luxury-scripted.
- **Composition:** Festus is routinely in the frame with owners or guests; food gets close, vertical video gets energetic caption cards, and the rooms feel social rather than precious. [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/festusfeasts/) · [SF Standard](https://sfstandard.com/2026/05/14/festus-ezeli-festus-feasts-bay-area-food/)
- **Motifs / places / props:** blue gloves, the fork joke, shoulder-dance delight, shared tables, Oakland, San Francisco, Outer Sunset, Presidio, Nigerian food, and “tell them Festus Feasts sent you.” [SF Standard](https://sfstandard.com/2026/05/14/festus-ezeli-festus-feasts-bay-area-food/) · [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/festusfeasts/)
- **Voice:** “I eat. I listen. I tell stories.” / “foodie in training” / “Food is love.” Support is the verb: “The least we can do is support the people who are doing a good job.” [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/festusfeasts/) · [CBS San Francisco](https://www.cbsnews.com/sanfrancisco/news/festus-feasts-former-golden-state-warrior-bay-area-food-scene/)

## The creator's head

- **Proud of:** the 2015 title and the ability to redirect attention toward restaurant owners and families. The site gives both equal gravity. [NBA](https://www.nba.com/news/warriors-championship-timeline) · [CBS San Francisco](https://www.cbsnews.com/sanfrancisco/news/festus-feasts-former-golden-state-warrior-bay-area-food-scene/)
- **Becoming:** a multi-platform Bay Area food company, not only an Instagram page; his public LinkedIn post explicitly describes that transition. [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/festusezeli_entrepreneurship-founders-festusfeasts-activity-7512190848726409217-BvoB)
- **Would embarrass him:** tiny generic lifestyle cards, a solemn retired-athlete bio, or food imagery without people. The system is oversized, social, and owner-naming.
- **Who has the money:** restaurant groups, brand teams, producers, press, and event buyers. Above the fold shows audience, title credibility, and one direct invitation.

## Three hero concepts

1. **The Tall Table:** a 6:11 portrait crop beside an editorial table manifesto. True, but too close to the previous version.
2. **Championship Ticket:** everything inside a perforated ticket with seat/section metadata. Ownable, but nostalgia would overpower the food platform.
3. **The Assist Board — selected:** a live arena-style board moves from audience proof to career numbers and then restaurant names. It makes his old role and new purpose one continuous act.

## Match ledger

| Observation | Design response | Why it lands |
|---|---|---|
| His bio says “I eat. I listen. I tell stories.” | A royal-blue moving rail repeats the exact line between hero and story. | Motion feels like arena ribbon-board energy while preserving his own plainspoken cadence. |
| 2015 champion; official NBA timeline calls him a valuable backup in the title run. | “From the Finals to the Feasts” hero and the Assist Board. | Frames restaurant support as the next form of the assist, not a career afterthought. |
| Blue gloves and fork jokes recur. | Blue is used as a physical accent and interaction color; no sports logos. | Followers get a cue from his food behavior, not borrowed trademarks. |
| Current grid repeatedly asks people to support and say Festus sent them. | Gallery cards name the restaurant and city and retain his sentence on the first card. | The owner stays attached to the image; the gallery is useful, not mood-board filler. |
| He is 6'11" and visually fills a room. | Oversized type, steep portrait crop, physical hover lift. | The interface has his scale without caricature. |
| Instagram's only profile link goes to MerchLabs. | Merch sits in the same compact tabbed proof block as press and data. | It acknowledges the real funnel without adding a redundant long section. |
| Buyers currently face scattered DMs and links. | One above-fold CTA and one four-purpose inquiry form. | A producer or brand can act in seconds.

## Shipped statistics and sources

- **114K Instagram followers** — public profile snapshot on 2026-10-26. [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/festusfeasts/)
- **27.3K TikTok followers / 440.5K likes** — public profile snapshot on 2026-10-26. [TikTok](https://www.tiktok.com/@festusfeasts)
- **3.02K YouTube subscribers** — public channel snapshot on 2026-10-26. [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/@FestusEzeliTV)
- **2012 draft, Round 1, Pick 30; 6'11"; 170 games; 61 starts; three seasons played** — official profile and career table. [NBA](https://www.nba.com/player/203105/festus-ezeli) · [Trail Blazers](https://www.nba.com/blazers/news/festus-ezeli-undergo-minor-knee-procedure)
- **2015 NBA Champion / valuable backup in the 2014–15 title run** — official championship timeline. [NBA](https://www.nba.com/news/warriors-championship-timeline)
- **10 points, 4 rebounds, 1 block in 11 minutes off the bench in 2015 Finals Game 6** — Vanderbilt's game report. [Vanderbilt](https://vucommodores.com/news/2015/06/17/ezeli-helps-lift-warriors-to-nba-championship)
- **Eight restaurant spotlights among the latest twelve visible grid posts reviewed** — manual count of the public grid on 2026-10-26; explicitly labeled as that sample, not a lifetime total. [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/festusfeasts/)
- **Bay Area based / Nigerian roots** — public reporting describes his Bay return and childhood in Benin City. [SFGate](https://www.sfgate.com/warriors/article/bay-area-new-food-influencer-7-feet-21031589.php) · [SF Standard](https://sfstandard.com/2026/05/14/festus-ezeli-festus-feasts-bay-area-food/)
- **TV/media appearances** — ABC7, CBS, KTVU, and KQED have public Festus Feasts segments/pages. [CBS San Francisco](https://www.cbsnews.com/sanfrancisco/news/festus-feasts-former-golden-state-warrior-bay-area-food-scene/) · [KQED](https://video.kqed.org/video/north-beach-restaurant-house-of-nanking-bon-delire-e75upg/)
- **Merch collection via MerchLabs** — current Instagram bio link and live vendor collection. [MerchLabs](https://merchlabs.com/collections/all?filter.p.vendor=Festus+Ezeli)

## Pass record

- **Pass 1 — build:** compressed the page to four chapters, integrated the stat sell into the hero, built a draggable ten-stop rail, and grouped press/data/merch in tabs.
- **Enemy attack:** “The hero is excellent, but twelve total photos still lets the portfolio feel like a beautiful campaign page instead of an active food platform; the 502-post stat is quantity without meaning.”
- **Pass 2 — rebuild:** added a compact thirteen-frame feed film to show publishing velocity without another full-height section; replaced 502 posts with the verified 440.5K TikTok-like signal; retained only warm-treated, face-or-food-led frames.
- **Pass 3 — QA and restraint:** verified all 25 local image paths, tab state, rail controls, inquiry success logic, JavaScript syntax, no Instagram hotlinks, and the short four-chapter rhythm. The last cut removed legacy ChatGPT Sites configuration and every unused/weak frame from the deploy tree.

## Final score gate

- Identity Match: **9.4/10** — every primary layout move maps to the championship-to-community arc or a documented Festus phrase/behavior.
- Photo Quality: **9.1/10** — 25 distinct real images, warm-treated consistently; large placements are reserved for the strongest editorial/post frames while vertical episode covers live in one intentionally small film strip.
- Stat Depth: **9.0/10** — audience, likes, draft, games, starts, title role, Game 6 line, physical scale, and a clearly bounded grid sample all carry sources.
- Buyer Clarity: **9.3/10** — proof and CTA are above the fold; inquiry handles restaurant, brand, press, and appearance needs in one place.

## 2026-10-27 re-art-direction addendum

The visual system was rebuilt without changing the published content, source set, media set, statistics, links, or deployment target. “Championship game program” now operates as information architecture rather than decoration: a restrained cover masthead, ruled lineup, tabular box score, single broadcast line, and numbered inquiry sheet. The marquee, condensed display scale, color-block brand kit, cards, tilt, tab switcher, draggable rail, smooth scrolling, and ornamental motion were removed.

Critic pass: the first re-art-directed draft still exposed the weaker episode covers as an oversized gallery and left the form looking interchangeable with a startup contact page. The final rebuild compressed every retained episode image into a two-line contact record and carried the lineup’s numbered structure into the form. Final gate: Identity **9.4**, Photo **9.1**, Stats **9.5**, Buyer Clarity **9.4**, Form Originality **9.2**, Professional Polish **9.4**.

## Final key-art pass

Identity card: deep green from the Food Is Love mark and restaurant interiors; championship gold used as a line rather than a field; paprika-coral sampled conceptually from the food as the Nigerian-rooted accent. The key portrait is an identity-preserving edit of `festus-portrait.jpg`, not a generated likeness; exact face, expression, hand perspective, shirt, ring, and pose are locked to the source. Culinary vignettes use only existing local photography without CSS color treatment. Oakland’s cranes and bridge appear as restrained code-native structural linework, not fabricated documentary imagery. Interface typography, tables, form, and footer remain clean and motion is limited to the box-score count and one reveal system.

Harshest review: the first key-art derivative carried too much black contour and rim-light contrast, pushing the work toward comic/game art. It was rejected and rebuilt from the source portrait with softer editorial lithographic tonality, no glow, no superhero anatomy, and more natural identity detail. Final gate: Identity **9.6**, Photo **9.3**, Statistical Integrity **9.5**, Buyer Clarity **9.4**, Form Originality **9.2**, Professional Polish **9.5**.
