# Creative decision record — 2026-10-27

## Evidence before aesthetics

The official biography separates broadcaster, foodie, creator and speaker. The primary Airbnb biography locates him in Benin City, migration at 14 and the Bay today. The podcast feed's latest release is March 2023: an archive, not an active weekly show. The collection's named garments connect food with language and family. Those facts suggest an editorial headquarters with hospitality as the organizing principle.

References inspected: The Modern (https://www.themodernnyc.com/) gives each dining experience its own reservation path; The Gentlewoman (https://thegentlewoman.co.uk/) separates a personality-led editorial library from commerce without severing their identity. Adopt clarity of paths and editorial hierarchy, not their layouts or assets. Research coverage is limited to these directly inspected references; no claim of exhaustive competitive study.

## Five competing directions

Scores below are design hypotheses, not user testing. Order: identity / originality / emotion / authenticity / commerce / photography / mobile / accessibility / maintenance / feasibility.

### 1. The Bay Area Field Guide
Thesis: Follow Festus through the Bay, one restaurant and one conversation at a time.
Architecture: places first; dinner, media and booking as supporting chapters. Hero: portrait beside a regional index. Narrative: map → people → dinner. Art: blue-slate cartography and orange route markers. Photography: owner-and-host pairs, food details. Type: a single humanist sans. Color: fog and orange. Interaction: geographic filters. Mobile: city-by-city itinerary. Conversion: watch a stop, visit a restaurant, book a meal. Weakness: reduces podcast and commercial work to an appendix.
Scores: 9 / 9 / 8 / 9 / 8 / 9 / 9 / 9 / 9 / 9 = 88/100. Lost because the geography can overshadow the man.

### 2. The Documentary
Thesis: A life rebuilt, told in three acts through portraiture, testimony and sound.
Architecture: chronological; actions at chapter exits. Hero: intimate full-screen portrait and a one-line premise. Narrative: Nigeria → championship → recovery → table. Art: cinematic crops, quiet captions. Photography: archival-to-contemporary progression. Type: serif display and neutral sans. Color: black, bone, restrained green. Interaction: one honors reveal. Mobile: short narrative spreads. Conversion: context first, actions later. Weakness: too much required reading before dinner or merch.
Scores: 9 / 9 / 10 / 9 / 7 / 10 / 8 / 9 / 9 / 8 = 88/100. Lost because narrative would tax a visitor's immediate intent.

### 3. The Modern Supper Club
Thesis: Festus hosts; the visitor gets a seat in his culinary and cultural world.
Architecture: dining leads; culture and commerce orbit it. Hero: a shared table with a clear reservation action. Narrative: invitation → menu of experiences → people. Art: intimate spatial compositions. Photography: tables, gestures and food at native scale. Type: warm serif plus disciplined small labels. Color: bone and slate with orange. Interaction: assemble an evening. Mobile: one-column reservation-first design. Conversion: strongest dining route. Weakness: overstates a continuously bookable hospitality business when availability is uncertain.
Scores: 8 / 8 / 9 / 8 / 9 / 10 / 9 / 9 / 9 / 8 = 87/100. Lost because the live listing cannot support the business promise implied by the concept.

### 4. The Cultural Publication
Thesis: A publication about the people who feed the Bay, edited through Festus's curiosity.
Architecture: stories, audio and film with a prominent commercial index. Hero: photographic cover with issue-like editorial hierarchy. Narrative: current features → origin note → deeper listening → actions. Art: asymmetrical spreads, no uniform cards. Photography: honest portraits and food, labeled video posters. Type: Georgia for authored headlines; system sans for controls. Color: fog, bone, slate, orange. Interaction: a personal reading/watch list. Mobile: compact publication index. Conversion: all four actions visible early. Weakness: could imply a newsroom or publishing cadence that does not exist.
Scores: 9 / 9 / 9 / 9 / 9 / 10 / 9 / 9 / 9 / 9 = 91/100. Runner-up; rejected the invented issue/cadence framing.

### 5. The Open Table — selected living headquarters
Thesis: One host, many ways in: the Bay's tables, his conversations, and the work that connects them.
Architecture: four immediate actions; three short-to-expansive acts; six persistent lanes. Hero: intimate half-width portrait opposite a precise headline and four-action index. Narrative: present identity → compact foundation → intimate rebuild/audio → expansive current work. Art: editorial spreads with orange as a directional signal, no posterized likeness. Photography: realistic, portrait-led, licensed original photographs only at release. Type: Georgia for human editorial voice; system sans for utilities, a justified two-role pairing with no font downloads. Color: bone/fog/slate/orange, gold only in honors, green only in rebuild. Signature: The Table Plan, a session-only shortlist connecting restaurants and their stories, copied with source links. Mobile: the same content order with a 6-item safe-area dock. Conversion: dinner/shop/watch/work immediately and at close. Weakness: depends on approved contemporary photography and a real contact system.
Scores: 9.5 / 9 / 9 / 9.5 / 9.5 / 9.5 / 9.5 / 9.5 / 9 / 9 = 93/100. Wins because present-day business stays legible without erasing the story. These are concept scores, not release scores.

## Signature mechanics

- **Home Ground:** city filters with a schematic Bay illustration, not claimed precise navigation. Semantic restaurant list remains primary. Touch: 48px buttons; no JS: full list. Cost: inline SVG and a small filter handler.
- **The Assist:** restaurant details disclose “Tell them Festus sent you.” This is a support invitation, not a partnership badge, discount or benefit. Native details works without JS; no animation required.
- **The Table Plan:** add verified stops, then copy a plain-text list with source links. Gives a fan a portable trail through Festus's discoveries. Touch/keyboard toggle buttons; live status; no persisted identity or location. Without JS, stop links and Assist remain usable. Cost: a few hundred lines of shared application code, zero libraries.
- **The Honors Reveal:** one restrained entrance of the historical record; reduced motion renders immediately. No repeat count-up, no game UI.

## Match ledger

| Evidence | Response | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Official site gives creator, broadcaster, food and speaker equal identities | Six lanes and four immediate actions | The current business is understandable before scrolling |
| Benin City → US at 14 → Bay, in first-person Airbnb biography | Compact origin paragraph, not a fabricated migration timeline | Specific without staging emotion |
| Injury inspired Rebuilding the Beast, official biography | Green listening chapter, dated archive, provider player on request | Reinvention is heard through his work |
| Actual Bay restaurants and owners drive Festus Feasts | Place names, explicit source links, geographic filtering | Place is useful information, not decoration |
| MerchLabs names food/family garments | Product names as concise commerce entry points | Language reflects actual merchandise |
| Live pricing and availability can change | Airbnb owns checkout and terms | Clear buyer path without invented scarcity |

## Release blocker acknowledged before implementation

Existing editorial photographs have no recorded commercial permission. Local review may show clearly identified candidate assets, but the release validator must fail until permissions and the 8–12-image requirement are satisfied. No new photo licenses, emails, or infrastructure purchases are authorized. No production replacement is allowed while binary gates fail.
