# Strategy — what this site is for

## The job

Nikhil asked "what's ur rate." This site is the answer that makes the rate
make sense: a finished creator site that looks like the work he sells —
cinematic, aerial-first, brand-ready — with the buying path built in.

## The funnel (Linktree, absorbed)

His link-in-bio page existed to route attention. The site absorbs every job
it did, natively:

| Linktree job | Where it lives now |
|---|---|
| Follow/watch on Instagram, TikTok, YouTube | Hero nav, Aerial "watch" strip, footer, close |
| Book/collaborate (Collabstr) | /kit (media kit) + /inquire (booking flow) — his own site, his own terms |
| Contact email | Footer, Story byline, Close, kit close |

Nothing on the site is a list of outbound buttons; each destination became
designed content or a working flow.

## The sell

- The kit carries his published packages ($250–$1,500) in rendered text —
  a brand can budget without a call.
- The inquiry form is anchored to those packages (content type + budget),
  so leads arrive pre-qualified: type, destination, timing, budget, contact.
- The numbers are all sourced to his own profiles — a brand-side reader
  (the toughest reader: a Meta PM) can verify every claim in two clicks.

## Handover (Zac's two questions, not site content)

1. Confirm the booking-routing email (built with his public
   nikhil@tootripsy.com).
2. Where the site should live — his own domain or ported.

Gate: the site sits behind basic auth (user nikhil) until Zac sends it;
the password travels with the link. SES note: the account's production
status is unconfirmed — if the first real inquiry delivery bounces in
sandbox, verify his address as an SES identity or request production
access at handover (a settings change, not a site change).
# Direction — TOOTRIPSY (Nikhil Gupta)

One-line: *Apple-keynote restraint over a drone reel.* The site behaves like a
film title sequence: the brand is the headline, the work is the argument, the
kit is the proof, the inquiry is two minutes.

## Pattern inherited from the Jalen build (~/chepheww)

- Same stack (Next.js static export, S3 + CloudFront, basic-auth gate, SES inquiry API).
- Same structure: brand-first hero → story-led work → proof → kit → inquiry → his footer.
- Same law: real photos first, sourced numbers only, nothing on the page that
  confesses it is anything but finished.

## Deliberate departures (the Taste Card, not the template)

| | Jalen | Nikhil |
|---|---|---|
| Temperature | warm tungsten, candlelight | cool blue-black, glacier |
| Type voice | Newsreader serif, light | Archivo grotesk, 800–900, tight |
| Motion | a dimmer that warms the page | settle + parallax; the loop does the moving |
| Accent | tungsten #C98A3D | aerial cyan #3FB9CF, sampled from his pools |
| Booking | dinner request (6 steps) | brand inquiry (4 steps, package-anchored) |
| Press layer | /press + one-pager | /kit — media kit with published packages |

## Voice rules

- Minimal, confident, short lines. No agency-speak, no adjectives doing the
  work his frames already do.
- His own words where possible: "storytelling, motion, and aerial
  perspectives" is his Collabstr bio, promoted to a headline.
- Never name a place or client beyond what his public profiles state.

## What the site must never do

- Show a stat that isn't in research/nikhil-brief.md or content/site.ts.
- Show a stock frame. Every image is his (agency/asset-sources.md).
- Carry any draft/review language, credit line, or process note.
# Design system — TOOTRIPSY

## Color

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| --ink | #07090C | dark ground (hero, work, close, footer) |
| --deep | #0B0F14 | raised dark (numbers band, form fields) |
| --slate | #131A21 | selected states on dark |
| --glacier | #EEF4F6 | light ground (brands, story, kit) |
| --fg-dark | #EEF4F6 | text on dark |
| --fg-dark-muted | #9DB1BB | secondary on dark |
